  "notes": "{引|ひ}き{出|だ}す is a compound verb meaning to pull/draw out.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Related noun: {引|ひ}き{出|だ}し (drawer)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- お{金|かね}を{引|ひ}き{出|だ}す (withdraw money)\n- {能力|のうりょく}を{引|ひ}き{出|だ}す (draw out ability)\n- {本音|ほんね}を{引|ひ}き{出|だ}す (draw out true feelings)\n\nMEANINGS:\n1. Physical: to pull something out\n2. Banking: to withdraw money\n3. Figurative: to elicit, bring out (potential, feelings)",
